It is Saturday morning.
The sun is shining over the city.
I go down to the street.
My neighbour, Nina, stands outside our building.
"Good morning, Maya," she says and smiles.
"Good morning, Nina," I answer.
"I have the day off today," I tell her.
"I am heading out into the city."
"Where are you going?" Nina asks.
"I am walking down to the water," I say.
"But I do not know the way."
Nina points down the street.
"Fortunately, it is very easy," she says.
"Go straight ahead here."
"And turn left at the park."
"Then you come right down to the harbour."
"Thank you very much for the help, Nina," I say.
"You are welcome, and have a good trip," she answers.
I wave to her.
I begin my walk towards the water.
